      "summaries": {
        "en": "Graphify is an AI coding assistant skill that transforms any folder of code, schemas, scripts, docs, images, or videos into a queryable knowledge graph. It integrates with tools like Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini CLI. Its key technical insight is using tree-sitter for precise code parsing and Leiden for graph clustering, enabling cross-domain understanding of app code, database schema, and infrastructure in one graph. Developers can instantly query complex codebases, uncover hidden dependencies, and accelerate onboarding or debugging by asking natural language questions against the graph.",
        "zh": "Graphify 是一个 AI 编码助手技能，能将任意包含代码、SQL 模式、R 脚本、Shell 脚本、文档、论文、图片或视频的文件夹转化为可查询的知识图谱。它无缝集成 Claude Code、Codex、OpenCode、Gemini CLI 等工具。其核心技术亮点是使用 tree-sitter 进行精确代码解析，并用 Leiden 算法进行图谱聚类，从而将应用代码、数据库模式和基础设施统一在同一图中。开发者可通过自然语言问答快速理解复杂代码库、发现隐性依赖，加速代码评审、调试或新成员入职。",
        "es": "Graphify is an AI coding assistant skill that transforms any folder of code, schemas, scripts, docs, images, or videos into a queryable knowledge graph. It integrates with tools like Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini CLI. Its key technical insight is using tree-sitter for precise code parsing and Leiden for graph clustering, enabling cross-domain understanding of app code, database schema, and infrastructure in one graph. Developers can instantly query complex codebases, uncover hidden dependencies, and accelerate onboarding or debugging by asking natural language questions against the graph.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "graphify stands out for antigravity, claude-code, and codex in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Graphify is an AI coding assistant skill that transforms any folder of code, schemas, scripts, docs, images, or videos into a queryable knowledge graph. It integrates with tools like Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini CLI. Its key technical insight is using tree-sitter for precise code parsing and Leiden for graph clustering, enabling cross-domain understanding of app code, database schema, and infrastructure in one graph. Developers can instantly query complex codebases, uncover hidden dependencies, and accelerate onboarding or debugging by asking natural language questions against the graph.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
